The correct semantics: SET variant = "gamma contained in the union J^-(I+)" vs parent single-q tail predicate "tail of gamma contained in J^-(q) for a single q". The single-q tail predicate entails the union reading (if a tail lies in J^-(q) for a single q then the curve lies in the union). The converse fails. So SET (union) is **strictly weaker** than the parent. Correct.

